---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, FEEDBACK_URL } from '../lib/links';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Skies"
  description="How the Skies Chrome extension and useskies.com handle your data: no account, no analytics, and your cities stay in your browser."
>
  <article class="container legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: September 24, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Skies is a world clock extension for Chrome. It doesn't have accounts, doesn't collect analytics, and doesn't
      sell or share personal data. This page covers what the extension stores and which outside services it contacts.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your city list, any names you give cities, their order, and your settings are saved in your browser's local
      storage. Skies also caches each city's sunrise and sunset times for the day. None of this is sent to us, and it's
      removed when you uninstall the extension.
    </p>

    <h2>Services Skies contacts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>City search.</b> The text you type in search is sent to the{' '}
        <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo Geocoding API</a> to find matching cities.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Sunrise and sunset.</b> The coordinates and time zone of each city you add are sent to the Open-Meteo
        Forecast API, about once a day, to pick the color of its card.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Flags.</b> Country flags in search results load from flagcdn.com.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These requests don't carry any identifier from Skies. As with any web request, these providers can see your IP
      address.
    </p>

    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      When you uninstall Skies, or choose Send Feedback in its settings, a <a href={FEEDBACK_URL}>Google Form</a> opens.
      Filling it in is optional. Anything you submit is collected by Google Forms and read by us to improve Skies.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      useskies.com doesn't use cookies or analytics. It's hosted on Cloudflare, which processes basic request data such
      as IP addresses to deliver and protect the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style lang="scss">
  .legal {
    max-width: calc(720px + var(--gutter) * 2);
    padding-top: clamp(48px, 8vw, 88px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 10vw, 112px);

    h1 {
      margin: 12px 0 8px;
      font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 48px);
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 40px 0 12px;
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    p,
    ul {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
    }

    p + p {
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    ul {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      padding-left: 20px;
    }

    b {
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    a {
      color: var(--color-logo-bottom);
    }

    &__updated {
      margin-bottom: 32px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
  }
</style>
